// Method Overriding ->
    Methods having same name , same return type , same parameter but perform different tasks
    and are defined in different classes .

    eg .   class Animal {
               void eat() {
                   System.out.println("Animal is eating");
               }
           }

           class Dog extends Animal {
               void eat() {
                   System.out.println("Dog is eating");
               }
           }

// Polymorphism ->
    It is an important concept of OOPs & defined as the ability of a message to be
    displayed in more than one form

    eg -> A person at the same time can have different characteristics like a man , at same time he is
    the father , a husband , a employee . so the same person for this different behaviour in different
    situations . This is called polymorphism .

